==Dutch==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈʋɪŋ.kəl/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-winkel.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|win|kel}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɪŋkəl|s=2}}
* {{homophones|nl|Winkel}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|winkel||corner}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|winkel}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*winkil}}, from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*weng-||to bend, bow, arch, curve}}.

Cognate with {{cog|de|Winkel}}, {{cog|ang|wincel}}. The meaning "shop" is derived from the meaning "corner in which merchandise is stalled".

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|m|-s|+}}

# [[shop]], [[store]] (establishment that sells goods to the public)
#: {{syn|nl|boetiek|handel|zaak|toko}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Ik ga naar de '''winkel''' om wat boodschappen te doen.|I'm going to the '''store''' to do some shopping.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Die '''winkel''' verkoopt de mooiste handgemaakte sieraden.|That '''shop''' sells the most beautiful handmade jewelry.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Er is een nieuwe '''winkel''' geopend in het winkelcentrum.|There's a new '''store''' that opened in the mall.}}
# a [[shop]], service point
# {{lb|nl|obsolete}} a [[corner]], as in [[winkelhaak]]

